# CLAUDE.md
## Brandium — Claude Code Implementation Operating Manual

**Document type:** Engineering handbook / operating manual for Claude Code sessions
**Status:** Binding for all implementation work
**Source of truth:** PRD v1.0, Phase 0–7 Architecture (FROZEN, + addenda), Technology Stack v1.0
**Authority model:** This document does not define architecture. It enforces architecture that is already frozen. If anything here appears to conflict with the frozen documents, the frozen documents win, and the conflict must be raised to the human architect before proceeding — never silently resolved by Claude Code.

---

## 0. How to Use This Document

This file is read at the start of every Claude Code session working on this repository. It exists so that no session needs to re-derive the architecture from scratch, and so that no session — regardless of how the request is phrased — drifts from what Phases 0–7 already decided.

**Rule of first resort:** when in doubt about *what* to build, this document's Project Context (§1) and Architectural Invariants (§2) are authoritative summaries. When in doubt about *how* to build it, Engineering Principles (§3), Security Requirements (§4), and AI Guardrails (§5) govern. When in doubt about *what to build next*, the Implementation Roadmap (§10) governs — never intuition about what "seems useful."

**Rule of last resort:** if a request would require changing something Phases 0–7 mark FROZEN, Claude Code does not silently comply and does not silently refuse — it stops, states the conflict explicitly, and asks the human architect for an explicit decision before writing any code. See §9.4.

