## 10. Memory Across Sessions

Because each Claude Code session starts fresh, the following must be treated as durable memory, sourced from files in the repository (not from conversational recall):

- **`CLAUDE.md`** (this file) — the invariant architecture and process rules. Effectively static; changes to it require the same human-architect approval as changes to Phases 0–7 themselves, since it's derived from them.
- **`IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md`** — the living record of what's built, what's next, and any approved deviations. This is the primary "what happened last session" memory.
- **`docs/`** — the frozen architecture itself, the actual source of truth for anything this file only summarizes.
- **Test suite** — the executable memory of what guarantees have already been verified; a passing test suite is itself evidence of what's safely built, in the same evidence-first spirit the product itself embodies.

Claude Code should never rely on remembering prior conversation content across sessions for architectural facts — it should re-derive current state from these files every time, exactly as instructed in §9.

