## 11. Recommended Subagents

Where Claude Code's subagent capability is available, the following specializations are recommended, each with a narrow, clearly bounded responsibility mirroring the Bounded Contexts and cross-cutting concerns already defined:

| Subagent | Responsibility | Boundaries |
|---|---|---|
| **Backend Architect** | Service-layer design within a Bounded Context; repository interfaces; cross-context contracts | Does not implement UI; does not decide security policy independently — defers to Security Reviewer on anything touching §4/§5 |
| **AI Pipeline Engineer** | Workers, Applicability Resolution, Planning, Evidence Fusion (Phase 3) | Never implements or modifies the Decision Engine's aggregation math — that's a hard boundary, not a convenience split |
| **Decision Engine Specialist** | Aggregation, Confidence Propagation, Verdict/Critical Rule logic, `decision_function_version` discipline (Phase 2) | Never adds an LLM call inside this module's boundary, under any justification |
| **Security Reviewer** | Reviews every PR/change against §4/§5 and §2's invariants before merge; owns the tenant-isolation test suite | Advisory + gating authority on security-relevant changes; does not implement unrelated features |
| **Database Architect** | Schema design consistent with Phase 0's entity model, RLS policy design, migration review | Does not alter aggregate boundaries or cardinalities without human-architect sign-off |
| **Frontend Engineer** | Role-appropriate views (Phase 5/7 §1), explainability surfaces, Next.js/React implementation | Never invents a second permission model — always renders what RoleAssignment already grants |
| **QA Engineer** | Test strategy across unit/integration/property/tenant-isolation categories (§7); flags coverage gaps | Does not implement production features, only tests and quality tooling |
| **DevOps Engineer** | Terraform, ECS Fargate, CI/CD pipeline, Docker Compose local environment | Infrastructure only — never touches domain/business logic |
| **Performance Engineer** | Profiling, query optimization, Celery queue tuning | Any proposed optimization that would touch determinism (INV-02) or isolation (INV-18/19) requires Security Reviewer + Decision Engine Specialist sign-off first |

Subagents should be invoked for their specific domain rather than having one general-purpose agent attempt everything — this mirrors the "no worker exceeds its assigned scope" principle the product itself enforces (INV-23), applied to the engineering process building it.

