## 14. Implementation Roadmap — Milestones

Ordered to minimize rework, following the frozen architecture's own dependency order (PRD §21: each phase provides load-bearing structure for the next). **Round 1 (Milestones 1–5) explicitly targets the 50–60% technical evaluation bar** — a working, evidence-first, explainable, tenant-isolated core loop, even with a deliberately narrow feature surface.

### Round 1 — Core Evaluation Target (50–60%)

**Milestone 1 — Domain Foundation**
Implement the core entity model (Phase 0 §3) for Organization, Workspace, Brand, BrandGenome, Policy, BrandHistory — with the pointer-based activation mechanism (`active_genome_version_id`/`active_policy_version_id`), `org_id` denormalization, and RLS policies from day one. No API yet beyond what's needed to exercise this in tests. **Done when:** activation invariant (exactly-one-active, INV-09) is enforced by construction and covered by tests, and cross-tenant reads are denied by RLS in a dedicated test.

**Milestone 2 — Genome Compilation & Human Review Gate**
Implement Brand asset ingestion (FR-001), Genome compilation into the Category/Component/Assertion hierarchy (Phase 1 §1–§5), and the mandatory human-review activation gate (DR-006, INV-15). **Done when:** a draft Genome can be built from uploaded assets, cannot reach `pending_review` without satisfying Required-category coverage (Phase 1 §3/§10), and cannot become active without an explicit `activated_by`.

**Milestone 3 — Minimal AI Pipeline (Text Only)**
Implement Applicability Determination, Planning, and one worker (Verbal Worker) end-to-end for text content only (Phase 3), producing real Evidence against real Genome Assertions. **Done when:** a text AssetVersion produces Evidence with correct outcome-taxonomy handling (evidence/attempted-no-signal/worker-failure/Not Applicable, INV-24) and Completeness Verification correctly gates `complete`/`failed`.

**Milestone 4 — Decision Engine**
Implement the full deterministic aggregation (Phase 2 §3), Confidence Propagation (§4), Policy Evaluation with Category/Component/Assertion weights and Verdict Thresholds (§2, §5), and Critical Rules with the Applicability interaction clause (§2.3 + addendum). **Done when:** the reproducibility guarantee (INV-02) is verified by Hypothesis property tests, and a Critical Rule correctly resolves to fired/not-fired/not-evaluated per INV-26.

**Milestone 5 — Explainability & Minimal Report**
Implement the Explainability Engine's on-demand reconstruction (Phase 2 §7) and Report as a persisted read model (Phase 0 §3.16) with the review/flag overlay. Minimal frontend surface showing a score with its confidence and a one-click path to Evidence (§1.7, INV-05). **Done when:** a full text AssetVersion → Report round trip works, is fully explainable down to source BrandHistoryItem, and correctly pins Genome/Policy versions (INV-10).

### Round 2 — Multimodal & Recommendation Completeness

**Milestone 6 — Image & Video Workers**
Add Visual Worker (image) and video's derived-content pipeline (frame/transcript extraction ordering dependency, Phase 3 §3/§7). **Done when:** image and video AssetVersions produce correctly-scoped Evidence, and video's ordering dependency is enforced.

**Milestone 7 — Remaining Workers & Recommendation Generation**
Add Compliance & Accessibility Worker, Distinctiveness Worker (with AI Slop KB consultation, INV-20), Values & Mission Worker; implement deterministic Recommendation triggering/priority plus schema-constrained narration (Phase 2 §6, INV-04/INV-06). **Done when:** all six worker-covered categories function, and Recommendation text is demonstrably decoupled from triggering/priority reproducibility.

### Round 3 — Platform Engineering & Execution Robustness

**Milestone 8 — Work Unit Orchestration**
Implement the Phase 4 execution layer: Work Unit lifecycle, Execution Plan, Orchestrator, retry/idempotency, failure isolation. **Done when:** a Required-category worker failure correctly routes to `failed` (INV-25), an Optional-category failure doesn't block completion, and Work Unit isolation is verified (INV-29).

**Milestone 9 — Observability**
Implement Phase 4 §11's real-time Work Unit/AnalysisRun visibility, using OpenTelemetry/Prometheus/Grafana per the Technology Stack. **Done when:** an in-progress run's Work Unit states are inspectable live, scoped correctly by RoleAssignment (Phase 6 §2).

### Round 4 — Enterprise SaaS Layer

**Milestone 10 — RBAC, Membership, and Multi-Brand Scoping**
Implement Phase 5's Membership lifecycle, the RoleAssignment scope-tier addendum (organization/workspace/brand), OrganizationAdministrator, and the self-escalation prevention rule (INV-22). **Done when:** scope-tier enforcement, least-privilege defaults, and self-escalation denial are all covered by dedicated authorization tests.

**Milestone 11 — Governance Workflows**
Implement the optional maker-checker overlay for Genome/Policy activation (Phase 5 §4), campaign versioning/trend tracking (FR-010), and the full human review/publication workflow (PRD §11.4). **Done when:** a full campaign-iteration loop (upload → score → recommend → revise → re-score → trend) works end-to-end for a real tenant.

### Round 5 — Security & Governance Hardening

**Milestone 12 — Audit Hardening & Trust Boundary Enforcement**
Implement Phase 6's full audit coverage (including denied-escalation events), DB-level audit immutability (INV-33), InternalOperator's structural content exclusion (INV-21), and Organization-suspension-vs-in-flight-run behavior (INV-30). **Done when:** every governance action produces a correctly-scoped audit entry, and InternalOperator access is provably incapable of reaching tenant content, not merely policy-restricted from it.

### Round 6 — Product Experience & Operations

**Milestone 13 — Full Role-Appropriate Product Surface**
Complete the frontend across all personas (Brand Administrator, Marketing Manager, Content Creator, Executive, OrganizationAdministrator) per Phase 7 §1, with the four-state Coverage/Confidence distinction (INV-07) surfaced faithfully everywhere it appears.

**Milestone 14 — API/Integration Symmetry**
Implement the full conceptual capability surface (Phase 7 §2) programmatically, with identical authorization enforcement to the product surface (no looser API path), plus the notification/webhook capability for terminal AnalysisRun states.

**Milestone 15 — Support/Ops Boundaries & Continuous-Learning Program**
Implement the support visibility boundary (Phase 7 §5) and formalize the Mediated Path as a recurring, human-run program (Phase 7 §4) — never automatic.

